WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.679
If you've been telling yourself,

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.080
>> I'll start in January, or I'll start on

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:05.759
Monday,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.759
>> I want you to hear this clearly. The

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:09.360
reason you feel behind, is because you

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:11.519
keep waiting to start, what are you

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.599
waiting for? Before we talk about growth

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:15.759
algorithms or posting schedules, we need

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.760
to talk about why most people quit, even

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:19.600
if they want to be a content creator,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.600
very badly. The biggest mistake that I

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.279
see content creators doing is trying to

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.600
create content around what they think

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:27.599
will perform well, rather than what just

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.199
kind of comes naturally to them, what

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.039
they're already automatically good at.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:33.040
So when it comes to starting your

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:34.719
YouTube channel, your Tik Tok page, etc.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.040
I want you to think about these three

00:00:34.719 --> 00:00:39.200
things first. One is who am I creating

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:42.160
for? It can actually be even helpful to

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.360
think of a specific person, a persona or

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.960
something like that that you can

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.399
actually visualize and answer these

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.760
questions. What are the problems that

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:49.440
they're solving in their day-to-day

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.039
life? Who do they hang out with? What

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.360
are their hobbies? Because that can all

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:55.120
lead you to this question here, which is

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.719
why would they want to watch your

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.800
videos? The second thing I want you to

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:01.520
ask yourself is what could I talk about

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.440
on end even if nobody ever watched. I

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.280
think that this is so important because

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.760
you are going to find more joy out of

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.240
creating videos that you like creating

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.240
that you find enjoyable that you find

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.920
interesting rather than what you think

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.240
other people want to watch. And then

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.640
lastly, think about what is the part of

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.040
content creation that I enjoy the most.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.600
It could be anything from coming up with

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.280
the ideas, doing research, actually

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.439
filming the content. Maybe it's

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.960
directing, could be editing, etc. So,

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:30.799
think about what is actually fun for you

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.560
and what you enjoy doing within the

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:34.079
content creation process. The reason I

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.560
want you to think about answers to those

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:38.960
questions is because passion is going to

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.479
be credentials every single time.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.000
Passion is always going to show through

00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:43.520
in your videos and the way that you talk

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.840
about your subject matter or the way

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.280
that you film, etc. Remember that you do

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.200
not need to be an expert. You do not

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.360
need years of experience. You just need

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.040
to be one step ahead of the person that

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.399
you are creating the content for. And I

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.560
also want to emphasize that I think

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:58.079
relatability is also powerful. People

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.920
want to watch videos from somebody

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:01.439
that's going through it with them. I

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.040
think a lot of the videos that have done

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:05.600
well on my channel are ones where I'm

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.080
sharing my exact income streams after

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.679
being laid off or my income streams as a

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.080
stay-at-home mom. And it's because those

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:14.000
are relatable things and taking other

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.200
people through that journey with me. And

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.720
if you're worried about your videos

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.160
being a little bit all over the place,

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.080
don't worry. I was definitely there,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.560
too. But clarity is going to come from

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.400
action rather than inaction. And in a

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.239
second, I will show you how to keep

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.080
going. Even if you feel like your niche

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:29.760
is a little bit unclear, remember that

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.680
right now as you're getting started,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.560
your job is not to be perfect. Your job

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.319
is to just start and feel aligned. Now,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.239
if editing is a reason that you are

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:39.760
intimidated by content creation or that

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:41.519
you're falling behind on your posting

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.319
schedule, etc. I need you to hear this

00:02:41.519 --> 00:02:46.239
very clearly. You do not need complex

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:48.959
edits to grow your YouTube channel. What

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:51.040
you do need is clear value in what

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:54.160
you're creating. You need captivating

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.080
titles, thumbnails, scripts, and maybe a

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.319
rough cut that kind of just helps keep

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.319
the pacing quick on your videos. And

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:01.440
then lastly, some clear audio so that

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:03.120
people watching your videos can

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.720
obviously hear you. But that's it. You

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.959
do not need tons and tons of fancy

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.800
edits. I know I personally hated the

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:10.400
editing process and I recently hired out

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.840
an editor because again, it was just

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.480
something that I personally did not

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.920
enjoy. But if you can't afford to hire

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.239
an editor yet at this point in your

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.840
YouTube career, a few tidbits or pieces

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:21.599
of advice that I have for you are cut

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.840
out things like filler words. If you say

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:25.599
um a lot or like, cut those out. Tighten

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.120
up your transitions. So again, the video

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:29.120
moves quickly and keeps the viewer

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.959
engaged. And then remember to always add

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.239
captions, not because it's trendy, but

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:34.319
because a lot of people actually watch

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:36.159
videos on mute. I personally do.

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:38.000
Captions also help hold viewers

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:39.599
attention, and they make your content a

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.519
little bit easier to consume. Remember,

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:43.120
things like music and sound effects are

00:03:41.519 --> 00:03:44.560
definitely optional. You definitely do

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.480
not need to have those. Of course, they

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.840
help keep your viewer engaged as well.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.920
But again, I just don't want you to get

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.760
caught up on the editing phase of

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.360
putting content out there because it

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.440
really is not as important as the other

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.519
pieces. If editing is taking you hours

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.200
and hours to do, you are trying to do

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:01.599
too much and that is what's going to

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.599
lead to burnout and inconsistency. So,

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:04.879
simplify your edits and your process in

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:06.879
general. And I'm actually going to go

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:08.480
into this more in just a second about

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.319
how you can simplify your overall

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.439
creation process to [music] keep you

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:15.040
from this start stop repeat cycle. So

00:04:13.439 --> 00:04:16.560
before I actually get into that, I just

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.880
quickly wanted to mention my mom to

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.880
monetized ebook. It is a full breakdown

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.639
step-by-step guide of what you should do

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.400
if you want to start a successful

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:26.720
YouTube channel. And it has everything

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.040
from starting from zero, coming up with

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.560
your niche, strong video ideas, all the

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.080
way through how to get to the point of

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.600
getting monetized. So, if you're curious

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.199
about that ebook, make sure you check it

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.800
out and also have it linked down in my

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:39.360
description box. Have you ever gotten

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.280
that sinking feeling when you don't know

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.880
what to post for your next video? That's

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.040
not a motivation problem. That's

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.720
actually a planning problem. So, let's

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.199
talk about how to plan your content that

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.199
is going to help you from stopping this

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:53.040
start, stop, repeat cycle. First off, I

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:55.120
want you to make your posting schedule,

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.199
your posting plan realistic. If we're

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.960
talking about YouTube, maybe this is two

00:04:57.199 --> 00:05:00.400
long form videos per week. Two videos

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.400
per week comes out to roughly eight

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.479
videos per month. That is a lot less

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.320
than 30 videos per month. Or posting

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:08.479
daily videos. That's just not realistic.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.080
Especially for me as a stay-at-home mom.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:11.520
My full-time job is taking care of my

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.039
daughter. I don't have time to post

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.960
every single day. In fact, I actually

00:05:13.039 --> 00:05:16.960
only post once per week because that is

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.720
just what is realistic for my lifestyle

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.880
and for my schedule. So, find whatever

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.800
is going to be realistic for you and

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.960
stick with it. And then the key here is

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.039
that you do need to dedicate actual time

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.039
to planning. Just like anything in life,

00:05:27.039 --> 00:05:30.960
planning is going to make your time and

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:32.400
your effort and your energy so much more

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.840
efficient. Let's be real. You're not

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.759
going to like show up to the airport

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.919
with absolutely no plan, no flight

00:05:35.759 --> 00:05:39.919
booked, no hotel booked, no idea where

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:41.520
you're going. That's just unrealistic.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:43.199
Maybe some of you would, but I wouldn't.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.960
I would come up with a plan and I would

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:47.840
have different things planned, right? To

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.240
make my vacation time more efficient,

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.000
fun, etc. Same thing goes for your

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.639
YouTube channel. It is going to be so

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.240
much more successful if you sit down and

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:57.919
do things like plan out your video

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.919
ideas, schedule out when you want to

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:02.479
post those, come up with video topics or

00:05:59.919 --> 00:06:04.479
titles, come up with scripts, etc. What

00:06:02.479 --> 00:06:06.080
I like to do is I actually will find

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:08.160
videos that are performing particularly

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.479
well within my niche, which is basically

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.080
called outlier research. I find videos

00:06:10.479 --> 00:06:14.400
that are considered outliers, you know,

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.400
strong performers that I can then use as

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.680
inspiration, make a video of my own

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.120
angle, my own lens on a similar concept.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.280
From there, I will make a laundry list

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:25.680
of video ideas, and then I will actually

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:28.479
schedule them out onto specific days for

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:30.160
posting at least like a month out. In

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:33.039
fact, I'm actually recording this in

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.720
December, so a month before this video

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:36.800
is going to go live. And what's going to

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:38.319
help you even more with continuing to

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.919
grow your YouTube channel is actually

00:06:38.319 --> 00:06:41.680
batching content. But I'm going to talk

00:06:39.919 --> 00:06:43.919
about that more in just a second.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.680
Planning is not optional if you want to

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:47.600
become a full-time content creator this

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.360
year in 2026. All right, let's talk

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:51.759
about batching content. Now, if you're

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.840
feeling exhausted every time that you

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:55.759
think about creating a video, then this

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.240
is probably part of your problem. If you

00:06:55.759 --> 00:07:00.000
have to constantly come up with a new

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.680
video idea, what to film, what you want

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.680
to say in your videos, that can actually

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:06.000
be very, very draining. In fact, this is

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.919
how I used to film my videos. I would

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.680
fall into this cycle of, okay, today I'm

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:12.000
filming, then tomorrow I'm going to

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.759
edit, and then the next day I'm going to

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.520
work on the thumbnail, and then finally,

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:17.440
oh, it's time to post. Okay, now it's on

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.919
the next week again. restart the cycle

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:22.960
of filming, editing, putting the video

00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:24.720
up on YouTube, posts, etc. It gets very

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.800
draining if you're constantly doing this

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:29.759
all the time. And it wasn't until I

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:31.759
started batching my content that I was

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:33.199
able to actually make my time a lot more

00:07:31.759 --> 00:07:35.759
efficient and even be able to give

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:37.360
myself time off. Yeah, I was for a while

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:39.520
there like not giving myself any time

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:41.360
off. Some benefits of batching content

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.599
is that it's going to help you stay in

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:45.840
the flow instead of having your time all

00:07:43.599 --> 00:07:47.840
choppy. You might be in, let's say, a

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.599
phase where you're focused on video

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:52.160
ideation. You can actually get into this

00:07:49.599 --> 00:07:54.000
flow of like finding strong video ideas

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.160
and coming up with your laundry list for

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.000
the next, let's say, month or 3 months,

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.080
etc. Rather than having it feel choppy

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.800
in every week, trying to come up with

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.639
and find new video topics. Same goes for

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:06.800
maybe scripting or filming. You kind of

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:08.319
get into this like flow state where you

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.599
get warmed up a little bit. you get

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:11.599
comfortable talking in front of the

00:08:09.599 --> 00:08:13.440
camera and it just feels a lot more

00:08:11.599 --> 00:08:14.960
natural. By doing all of the planning,

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.639
sitting down and doing the research and

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.240
all of that, you're going to know that

00:08:16.639 --> 00:08:20.240
whatever you posted had strong

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.160
convection behind it. So, there's no

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.919
reason to worry about if it should

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.680
perform well or not. And most

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:27.599
importantly, batching content will help

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.360
you actually create a bit of a buffer.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:30.960
So, in case you didn't know, I'm

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:33.200
actually pregnant and I'm trying to

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:36.080
actually batch my content ahead of time

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.880
right now so that I can essentially take

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:41.120
a month or two off with my newborn baby

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.839
and still have content being posted

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.440
while I'm on maternity leave. So, that's

00:08:43.839 --> 00:08:47.760
another benefit to batching your

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:49.760
content. Whether it's having a baby,

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.680
going on vacation, or what have you,

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.920
batching your content will help you

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:55.760
create a buffer in case life happens.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.360
So, here's an example of kind of how my

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.360
monthly schedule looks with batching

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:01.600
content. First of all, week one, we have

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.000
doing our research. This means coming

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.600
through YouTube or Vid IQ I use a lot of

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.440
times, too, to find videos that are

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.360
performing particularly well within my

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.360
niche. I'll also look back at my own

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.360
videos that have performed well and see

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.800
if there's any ideas within those that I

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:19.839
can tweak a little bit, improve on, or

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:22.800
recycle. I will then also select my

00:09:19.839 --> 00:09:24.959
exact video titles and schedule them out

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.519
for the next month or maybe even two

00:09:24.959 --> 00:09:29.440
months. Then during week two, I will go

00:09:27.519 --> 00:09:32.000
through and I will start scripting all

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.760
of my videos. So yeah, if I have four

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.080
videos, I will sit down and script all

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:38.399
four of them at once so that when I go

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.560
on to the filming phase, I don't have to

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:42.240
kind of guess at what I want to say,

